WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:04.970
When it comes to comic book movies, fans have
an insatiable appetite for scraps of news

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:07.320
about what might happen to their favorite
superheroes.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:12.100
And considering the super-cemetery we got
at the end of Avengers: Infinity War, it's

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:16.260
probably no big surprise that Marvel movie
fanatics are even hungrier for news about

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:17.920
the highly anticipated follow-up.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:22.220
That's why we're spinning up the rumor mill
once more to see what the Russo brothers have

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:23.700
in store for Avengers 4.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:28.860
Want to avoid finding out what might happen
in the next Avengers movie and the whole MCU?

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:30.460
"Spoiler alert."

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:33.080
Then you shouldn't have clicked on this video,
you big dummy!

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.060
The death of Tony Stark

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:40.360
One Redditor claiming to have connections
with, quote, "a reliable source," has reportedly

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:44.800
been told that Spider-Man: Far From Home will
open with Peter Parker mourning the loss of

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:46.100
his mentor, Tony Stark.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:51.100
According to the Reddit post, the movie's
plot will revolve around stolen Stark technology

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:52.660
that Spidey has to retrieve.

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:56.820
Whether the Reddit post is the real deal or
not, it wouldn't be much of a surprise to

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:58.460
predict Tony Stark's demise.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:03.420
As Marvel fans all know, Robert Downey Jr.'s
contract with Marvel Studios is finished after

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:08.080
Avengers 4, so the longest-serving member
of the MCU may go out in a blaze of glory

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:08.800
as a result.

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:13.160
Could you think of a better way to retire
from being a superhero than biting the dust

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:14.220
to save the world?

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:15.280
Didn't think so.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:17.740
Sorry, didn't mean to say 'dust'.

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:19.980
Pepper Potts suits up

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:25.120
Ever since Pepper Potts briefly donned Iron
Man's Rescue Armor in Iron Man 3, fans have

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:27.700
been dying to see her suit up and join the
action again.

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:32.100
She came to Stark's aid during the attack
on his Malibu mansion, proving herself more

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:34.480
than able to slip into some armor and help
out.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:39.020
Given that half of everyone Tony knows has
suddenly disintegrated, Stark is going to

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:42.560
need all the help he can get as he attempts
to undo what Thanos has done.

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:49.160
So will Pepper Potts be among the new recruits?

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:52.260
Gwyneth Paltrow's Instagram suggests she will
be.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:57.240
In a 2017 post that the actress has since
made private, Paltrow shared a potentially

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:01.799
spoilery picture of herself getting a foot
massage on set, which also revealed she was

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:04.640
clearly wearing a motion capture suit on her
legs.

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:10.080
She didn't turn up in any kind of GCI getup
in Infinity War, so the only logical explanation

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:12.800
is that she was filming scenes for Avengers
4 at the time.

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:17.660
The actress all but confirmed this was the
case during her 2018 appearance on The Late

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:18.760
Show with Stephen Colbert.

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:23.940
"When you were working on the movie did you
thrust your hand towards someone wearing like

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:26.520
a blue suit with ping pong balls glued on
it?"

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:27.980
"Yes!"

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:30.280
Is Nebula the main villain?

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:36.380
Nebula, played by Karen Gillan, has been on
the periphery of events so far, but the daughter

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:40.410
of Thanos could turn out to be a crucial player
in Avengers 4, with her arc potentially coming

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:41.060
full circle.

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:45.780
She started out hating her adopted sister
Gamora, but they reconciled before Gamora

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:48.380
was killed by their so-called father in Infinity
War.

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:53.920
The third Avengers outing borrowed heavily
from 1991's Infinity Gauntlet comic book series,

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:56.320
and Nebula plays a huge part in its conclusion.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:02.340
In the six-issue story, Nebula is captured
by Thanos and sadistically tortured, a moment

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:05.120
we've already seen play out on screen in Infinity
War.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:09.500
She's the one who's eventually able to turn
the tables on Thanos, stealing the Gauntlet

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:10.000
from him.

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:15.480
The problem is, Nebula is so messed up at
this point that she ends up being even worse

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:19.750
than Thanos with the Gauntlet, forcing the
intergalactic warlord to team up with the

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:21.240
Avengers in a bid to stop her.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:25.290
Gillan has dropped hints in the past about
the films potentially staying true to the

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:25.980
source material.

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:29.030
She explained in a 2017 interview with ScreenRant:

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:33.300
"When I was preparing to play Nebula the first
time, I read The Infinity Gauntlet.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:36.940
I loved it because it was like the most Nebula-heavy
comic."

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:41.000
She added that it would be amazing if the
movies were to follow the same arc, and said,

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.240
"I don't know yet, very big secret.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:44.120
But I'm hoping."

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:46.220
Shuri steps up

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:51.300
Wakanda made a valiant attempt to halt Thanos'
invasion of Earth in Infinity War, but the

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:56.460
fictional African nation sustained devastating
losses in the process, and that was before

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:58.440
the Mad Titan even used the Infinity Gauntlet.

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:03.460
King T'Challa was one of the unlucky souls
turned to dust when Thanos snapped his fingers,

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:06.660
leaving Wakanda without a leader going into
Avengers 4.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:12.200
The stage seems set for T'Challa's younger
sister Shuri, played by Letitia Wright, to

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:16.700
accept the Black Panther mantle and rally
her people for round two with Thanos.

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:19.140
This exact thing has happened in the comics.

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:25.500
In Reginald Hudlin's 2009 Black Panther series,
T'Challa falls into a coma after a battle,

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:27.980
and Shuri takes over as the hero of Wakanda.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:32.880
It's a premise that could certainly unfold
in the planned Black Panther sequel, or Avengers

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:33.380
4.

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:36.960
Wright herself has expressed an interest in
following Hudlin's story.

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:39.080
She told ScreenRant in 2018:

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:41.920
"If the opportunity came about, then why not?

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:43.340
It would be comic book accurate.

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:44.820
Yeah, that would be amazing.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:49.060
It means more training, more learning and
it would really be an amazing adventure.

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:49.860
[...] I'm excited!"

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:54.440
Recently revealed concept art from the first
Black Panther movie confirms early designs

00:04:54.449 --> 00:04:59.070
for Shuri's Black Panther outfit already exist,
so it's starting to look like a matter of

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:01.600
when she'll become the new Black Panther,
not if.

00:05:02.140 --> 00:05:03.420
Loki fakes his death?

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:04.660
Again?

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:08.120
Back in Thor: The Dark World, we saw Loki
fake his death.

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:12.480
And plenty of Marvel fans think that was just
a preview of him pulling it off again in Infinity

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:14.400
War, despite Thanos saying:

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:16.340
"No resurrections this time."

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:21.940
In fact, leaked set photos seem to confirm
that Tom Hiddleston will indeed return as

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:27.060
Loki for Avengers 4 in some capacity, though
whether these images reveal a flashback or

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:29.620
some kind of time travel mechanics is anybody's
guess.

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:32.320
Red Skull and the Infinity Stones

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:37.140
Not many people expected to see Red Skull
pop up in Infinity War, but it turns out the

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:41.900
-sympathizing villain could have closer
ties to the MCU's overarching plot than we

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:42.400
realized.

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:48.160
Real name Johann Schmidt, the former HYDRA
boss was the main antagonist in 2011's Captain

00:05:48.169 --> 00:05:52.169
America: The First Avenger, but he vanished
at the end of that movie after touching the

00:05:52.169 --> 00:05:53.440
Tesseract with his hands.

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:57.440
His whereabouts became a mystery, but we know
exactly where he ended up.

00:05:57.660 --> 00:06:02.140
When Thanos arrives on Vormir in search of
the Soul Stone in Infinity War, he discovers

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:04.620
that Red Skull has become the stone's guardian.

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:07.160
"I too sought the stones.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.960
I even held one in my hand.

00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:14.440
But it cast me out, banished me here."

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:19.500
Thanos acquires the Soul Stone by sacrificing
the person he loves most, Gamora.

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:23.340
Now that he has it, is Red Skull free to go
about his business?

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:27.910
According to the Russo Brothers, he is, and
his hunt for the Infinity Stones might not

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:28.400
be over.

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:33.960
As part of Vudu's Infinity War viewing party,
the Russo Brothers took questions from fans,

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:36.020
one of whom asked about Red Skull's future.

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:36.840
They explained:

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:42.300
"Red Skull is free to leave Vormir, and he
is also free to pursue his desire for an Infinity

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:42.800
Stone."

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:45.640
So could he still have a part to play in Avengers
4?

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:47.480
Avengers: End Game?

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:52.860
In June 2018, hint-hungry fans noticed that
cinematographer Trent Opaloch had added the

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:57.160
fourth Avengers movie to the credits section
of his personal website, casually dropping

00:06:57.160 --> 00:07:00.060
what appears to be the title of the movie
in the process.

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:04.820
Opaloch, who worked with the Russo Brothers
on Captain America: The Winter Soldier, Captain

00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:09.630
America: Civil War and Avengers: Infinity
War, listed the upcoming Marvel tentpole as

00:07:09.630 --> 00:07:15.060
Avengers: End Game, a title that might have
just been foreshadowed on a few other occasions.

00:07:15.380 --> 00:07:19.360
A post on The Independent points out that
the phrase "end game" has popped up in a few

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:20.820
Marvel movies before now.

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:24.960
For example, there was Tony Stark's angry
monologue in Age of Ultron:

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:26.000
"We're the Avengers.

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:30.680
We can bust arms dealers all the live-long
day but that up there, that's...that's the

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:32.780
end game."

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:39.820
Then, there was Doctor Strange talking to
Tony after he gives Thanos the Time Stone

00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:40.660
in Infinity War:

00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:42.700
"Why did you do that?"

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:48.320
"We're in the end-game now."

00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:56.300
Opaloch has since deleted the "End Game" part
of the title and now has the movie listed

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:57.820
simply as Avengers 4.

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:02.840
But let this be a lesson to all you aspiring
cinematographers, if you're working on one

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:07.090
of the biggest movies in the world, maybe
check with your bosses before you update your

00:08:07.090 --> 00:08:07.939
online resume.

